acceptance_criteria: "A generation without both a proxy and a held-out score cannot be promoted; both scores carry objective id, objective version and evaluation context, attributed to the same standard; every objective declares a direction and the gap is computed direction-aware so a positive gap always means proxy ahead of held-out; scores whose objectives declare no comparable scale are refused rather than compared; the gap, its per-generation delta and the window comparison are computed over one explicitly selected ancestry; a widening gap over the configured window is surfaced as a named finding rather than left for a reader to notice; the held-out score is always attributed to the pinned environment version and seed set that produced it"
resolution: Added test/lineage.test.ts exercising the direction-aware proxy-to-held-out gap and its trend.
expected_result: Both scores are attributed to one standard; the gap is direction-aware; widening over the window is a named finding; deltas are per-ancestry.
actual_result: test/lineage.test.ts passes; index.ts and lineage.ts at 100/100/100 lines/branches/functions.
